1
00:00:18,935 --> 00:00:22,771
We have seen a star in the east.

2
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:29,194
It told us the Son of God is born.

3
00:01:01,019 --> 00:01:04,897
NATIVITY PLAY - SERMON - DINNER

4
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,858
The Lord Jesus
was laid in a manger

5
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:11,653
to bring salvation
to the souls of those

6
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,990
with no place of their own.

7
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:18,285
Nothing is harder
than to have no place

8
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:22,498
but many are those without one.

9
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:23,874
Tell me about it!

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,336
In their solitude,
they long for someone who will say:

11
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:28,837
"I want you to be here."

12
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,422
Not me, thanks.

13
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:31,882
Be quiet!

14
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:37,429
Jesus was born to offer those alone
a place in which to be alive!

15
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,726
"Joy to the world,
the food has come."

16
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:45,395
Gin! It's "the Lord has come"!

17
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,856
You don't know much, do you?

18
00:01:47,982 --> 00:01:50,526
More than some queer.

19
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:54,029
I am a mistake made by God.

20
00:01:54,155 --> 00:01:56,824
In my heart, I am a woman.

21
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,826
Women can have children.

22
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:02,830
What if a miracle like
the Virgin Mary getting pregnant

23
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,624
was to happen to a queer?

24
00:02:06,126 --> 00:02:12,297
Better give me a little extra.
After all, I'm eating for two.

25
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:38,240
Serves you right!

26
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:42,452
Miyuki!

27
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:45,706
Time to eat!

28
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:51,003
Miyuki!

29
00:02:51,129 --> 00:02:54,423
Close your legs!
Act like you were a woman.

30
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:55,757
I am a woman.

31
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:58,760
And it's a waste
to spill food like that.

32
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,514
Don't just gobble your bread.

33
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:07,477
Eat it with love for the people
who made and brought it here.

34
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:11,899
I hate that Bible-thumping.
You're just like Akiko.

35
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,358
Who's Akiko?

36
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,153
My old lady.

37
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,279
Well!

38
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:19,239
Don't call your mother that.

39
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:21,742
Eat shit, you old fart.

40
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:24,119
"Shit" I'll take, but "fart" I won't!

41
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:26,079
That hurts! You old...

42
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:28,457
"bag lady."

43
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:33,587
You peep pretty loud for a chick
that can't even find its own worms.

44
00:03:33,713 --> 00:03:37,049
Should a burden on society like you
be talking?

45
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:41,178
You're a burden on us.
What does that make you?

46
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,973
The kettle the pot's calling black!

47
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:48,185
You mouthy brat!

48
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:52,564
Can't you at least get along
at Christmas?

49
00:03:53,149 --> 00:03:56,193
Oh, yes.
Miyuki, I got you a present.

50
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:00,948
They're gone!

51
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:04,284
A whole set of
"World Literature for Children".

52
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,912
Why would I need that?

53
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:08,872
Hana looked hard for those!

54
00:04:08,998 --> 00:04:13,001
Even a homeless teenage runaway
needs a Christmas present!

55
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,588
I choose not to go home.

56
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:20,217
Six months on the street
means you don't have a home.

57
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:23,220
I can go home any time I want to.

58
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:26,890
It's the ones who say that
who never do.

59
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:29,059
Speak for yourself, you old geezer!

60
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:32,396
What are you doing to Dostoevsky?

61
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,775
I won't take that, today of all days!

62
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:41,238
Not even my father ever hit me!

63
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:45,117
So I'll do it for him!

64
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:51,415
Grow up, will you?

65
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:53,959
Don't hurt yourselves.

66
00:04:54,752 --> 00:04:56,461
Show more respect, kid!

67
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:58,130
I'm not a kid!

68
00:04:58,256 --> 00:05:00,841
With little tits like these?

69
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:03,135
You filthy old pervert!
That's harassment!

70
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:05,178
Will you two stop?

71
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:09,224
Huh?

72
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:30,329
It's been...

73
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,788
...abandoned.

74
00:05:32,457 --> 00:05:34,458
There, there, there.

75
00:05:37,211 --> 00:05:39,338
CARE FOR THIS CHILD.

76
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:45,260
What a world! Oh, man!

77
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:49,848
Oh, my! You're a little girl.
I wonder what your name is.

78
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:51,641
"John Doe."

79
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:53,935
She's a girl, I said!
He's so rude!

80
00:05:54,771 --> 00:06:00,317
How old was I when I started
living like this? Thirty-something?

81
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:08,742
I still thought that I was better off
than a child with no home.

82
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:20,712
There, there, now!
We'll take you somewhere warm.

83
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:25,425
The cop shop's that way!

84
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:30,347
This is a Christmas present
from God!

85
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:33,308
She's our baby!

86
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:34,643
Huh?

87
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:49,032
A TOKYO GODFATHERS COMMITTEE
PRODUCTION

88
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:55,914
DEVELOPED BY MASAO MARUYAMA
ORIGINAL STORY BY SATOSHI KON

89
00:06:56,833 --> 00:07:00,252
SCREENPLAY BY
KEIKO NOBUMOTO & SATOSHI KON

90
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:05,632
CHARACTER DESIGN:
KENICHI KONISHI & SATOSHI KON

91
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:09,553
ANIMATION DIRECTOR:
KENICHI KONISHI

92
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:13,640
ART DIRECTOR: NOBUTAKA IKE
COLOUR DESIGN: SATOSHI HASHIMOTO

93
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:15,100
CO-DIRECTOR: SHOGO FURUYA

94
00:07:15,226 --> 00:07:17,227
DIRECTOR OF PHOTOGRAPHY:
KATSUTOSHI SUGAI

95
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:22,607
MUSIC: KEIICHI SUZUKI
SOUND DIRECTOR: MASAFUMI MIMA

96
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:26,361
Sorry!

97
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:29,406
What do you mean,
take her with us?

98
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:32,117
I'm just doing God's will.

99
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:34,369
Her parents might come back.

100
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:38,123
What parent would leave
a child out in this cold?

101
00:07:38,249 --> 00:07:40,917
That's a devil, not a parent!

102
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:47,299
Kiyoko wanted us to find her.

103
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:48,633
"Kiyoko"?

104
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:51,261
"Kiyoko"? Why "Kiyoko"?

105
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:55,599
From kiyo, "pure,"
on this purest of nights.

106
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:59,478
- How tacky!
- Kiyoko's a fine name!

107
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:01,980
Did you have
a girlfriend named that?

108
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,732
Idiot!

109
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:08,695
Look, we can't just name her!
She's not a puppy or a kitten!

110
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:10,322
So I'm taking her home.

111
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,823
To a cardboard box?

112
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,783
There's no room!

113
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:18,955
This is a once-in-a-lifetime chance!
Let me feel like a mother!

114
00:08:22,084 --> 00:08:23,710
A haiku:

115
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:30,634
"A little baby, powdery snow
on its cheeks, on this holy night."

116
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,679
DIRECTED BY SATOSHI KON

117
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:48,276
Peek-a-boo!

118
00:08:50,238 --> 00:08:52,614
Oh, dear! Tell me what's wrong!

119
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,282
Shut up!

120
00:08:58,579 --> 00:08:59,204
Hey!

121
00:08:59,330 --> 00:09:04,084
I know, I know, he's not your mommy.
He's just a homeless homo.

122
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,878
Don't say that in front of her!

123
00:09:07,004 --> 00:09:10,882
A baby crying around here
will sound weird!

124
00:09:11,008 --> 00:09:14,261
We're going to take you
to the police soon, okay?

125
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:16,805
You're not going anywhere, are you?

126
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:19,641
Idiot! We're taking her to the police!

127
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,935
Don't shout or she'll never shut up!

128
00:09:22,061 --> 00:09:25,480
Why won't you stop crying?
Are you hungry?

129
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:26,606
There, there!

130
00:09:26,732 --> 00:09:29,150
Maybe she's sick.

131
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:46,585
Tomorrow.
I promise I'll take her then.

132
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:52,340
Christmas should be
the happiest day of the year.

133
00:09:52,466 --> 00:09:55,844
If we take her in now, it'll always be
the worst day of her life!

134
00:09:57,555 --> 00:10:01,266
Maybe... she needs a diaper.

135
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,194
Hana, boil some water.

136
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:14,904
I'll make some milk.

137
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:17,324
Hey! Whose side are you on?

138
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:22,078
Go buy some water!
My angel isn't drinking from the tap!

139
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:23,913
Why me?

140
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:29,919
Where does a bum get off telling me,
"Them that works eats"?

141
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:36,676
Just for tonight, remember.
Tomorrow we take her to the police.

142
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:43,058
So "no man is an island"
after all, huh?

143
00:10:47,104 --> 00:10:49,189
You're buying water?

144
00:10:50,107 --> 00:10:52,067
A Christmas miracle.

145
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:54,694
What a haul!

146
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:03,578
Watch where you're going, brat!

147
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:05,914
You watch where you're going!

148
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,586
I was married once.

149
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:13,505
With a child?

150
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:17,175
No, don't tell me.
I don't want to hear this!

151
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:22,055
You never forget for one second.

152
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:26,601
A child's the only thing
you hold dearer than life itself.

153
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:29,688
A boy?

154
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:31,106
No.

155
00:11:36,028 --> 00:11:37,570
Bullshit!

156
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:39,406
Come on! Give it back!

157
00:11:39,532 --> 00:11:44,035
Hey, you're the girl
who hangs out with Gin.

158
00:11:44,161 --> 00:11:45,829
Get out of here, will you?

159
00:11:45,955 --> 00:11:50,542
- We don't want Gin after us.
- Why not?

160
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:54,587
You're the light of his life,
that's why not!

161
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:59,926
There's not much light
in a cardboard box.

162
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:02,262
Let me have this book.

163
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,850
How old?

164
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:09,227
Twenty-one, I think.

165
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:13,898
Five or six years older than Miyuki,
I guess.

166
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:15,859
That old?

167
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,403
If she was alive.

168
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:24,951
When I was 20, I got a girl pregnant
and we got married.

169
00:12:25,077 --> 00:12:27,370
I was in heaven.

170
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:31,374
You could have poked me in the eye
and I'd have just smiled at you.

171
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:37,547
But my daughter got sick,
and the medical bills were huge.

172
00:12:37,673 --> 00:12:41,926
I was something
of a bicycle racer then.

173
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:46,431
I needed money.
There was this race...

174
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:48,183
You threw it?

175
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:54,314
A punk I knew had this scheme.

176
00:12:54,440 --> 00:13:00,278
They found out, I got kicked out
of racing, and my girl died.

177
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:03,656
I just didn't feel like working anymore.

178
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:06,910
And then my wife followed my daughter.

179
00:13:07,036 --> 00:13:08,119
Oh, no!

180
00:13:09,538 --> 00:13:12,207
That's how you get to be a man like me.

181
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:15,752
I didn't want to hear that.
I hate sad stories!

182
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:19,088
It's freezing!

183
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:26,179
- You're used to this.
- Kind of.

184
00:13:26,305 --> 00:13:28,264
I'll give her the milk.

185
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:31,142
Dreams do come true.

186
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:36,064
I always dreamed of being
the mother of a little girl.

187
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:38,525
A nice, warm house, a pretty daughter.

188
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:41,361
Even if my husband was no good,

189
00:13:41,487 --> 00:13:44,531
I would accept dire poverty
as long as I had my child.

190
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,699
Feed the poor kid!

191
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:53,581
You're so pretty.

192
00:13:54,375 --> 00:13:58,086
The prettiest little girl in the world.

193
00:14:23,445 --> 00:14:25,154
What do you want?

194
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:26,573
They're gone.

195
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:31,995
Santa Claus, maybe?

196
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:35,290
"Uncle Bag" and the baby are gone.

197
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:38,167
What's that queer thinking about?

198
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:43,548
Man, he's got big feet!

199
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:45,967
You can't have feet fixed.

200
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,944
Are you taking her back?

201
00:15:06,363 --> 00:15:09,032
There's probably an APW out on her.

202
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,659
- And for you.
- I doubt it.

203
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:15,705
An arrest warrant, maybe.

204
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:20,376
Her parents are probably
sorry about this now.

205
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:22,754
So let's take her to the police.

206
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:27,842
A baby's always better off
with its real mother.

207
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:29,719
Not necessarily.

208
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:34,474
Sometimes a foster mother's better.

209
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,935
- What?
- Don't be stupid.

210
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:40,939
I never knew my real mother.

211
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:47,570
But I'll bet if she saw me now, she'd flip.

212
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:51,824
How can someone homeless
raise a child?

213
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,452
I know, I know!

214
00:15:55,537 --> 00:15:59,415
I don't want her shunted
from one foster home to another

215
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:04,337
without even one memory
of ever having been loved.

216
00:16:04,463 --> 00:16:08,132
You don't have to be a foundling
to feel that.

217
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:10,593
They must have had their reasons.

218
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:13,513
Nothing should make you
abandon a child!

219
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:20,103
That means you've taken love
and tossed it away, like trash.

220
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:24,524
Yeah, but what can we do about it?

221
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:26,651
Find her mother.

222
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:31,948
And ask why she abandoned her baby.

223
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:35,785
If she can make me understand,

224
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:39,247
I'll forgive her,
and my mother too.

225
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:42,291
Find her?

226
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:44,002
How?

227
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:50,049
We'll have to pay again.

228
00:16:50,634 --> 00:16:53,928
This is an expensive year-end!

229
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,264
What if we find another baby?

230
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,933
They don't toss them out in twos.

231
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:12,030
Another key!

232
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:16,117
Look at these panties.
You'd catch cold in them!

233
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:19,328
Are they the ones?

234
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:24,917
Are these your folks?

235
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:27,211
Look, business cards.

236
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:38,181
A hostess club won't be open
at this hour.

237
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,059
We've got some walking to do.

238
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:43,436
You've gotta be kidding!

239
00:17:46,732 --> 00:17:48,608
He was eating for two!

240
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:07,585
But why pack like you're off on a trip
and then abandon a baby?

241
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:11,422
Maybe it was one last trip
they were taking.

242
00:18:11,548 --> 00:18:13,925
A family suicide?

243
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:18,387
Then what do we do?
We can't search the next world.

244
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:19,972
Shh!

245
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:29,190
We apologise
for any inconvenience.

246
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:33,194
Trains will be delayed
due to heavy snowfall.

247
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:36,239
It's so hot in here!

248
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:38,074
What a stink!

249
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:41,619
Have you bathed lately?

250
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:44,247
No. Or washed my clothes.

251
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,998
How embarrassing!

252
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:58,052
Oh, dear! There, there.

253
00:18:58,178 --> 00:19:01,597
Did she piss herself?
That's why it stinks.

254
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:03,558
It's you that stinks!

255
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:06,686
- Quiet!
- Shut that kid up!

256
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:23,953
- Watch it!
- Hey!

257
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:36,465
- Miyuki!
- What's she up to?

258
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,474
We wasted our train fares.

259
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,519
It was me who paid them.

260
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:53,524
I'm sorry, there's no more milk.

261
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:56,277
Go ahead, blame it all on me.

262
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:59,572
Oh, cheer up! Let's sing a song.

263
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,411
What's that?

264
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:08,289
- The Sound of Music, of course.
- Never heard of it.

265
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:19,926
That's going to make you even hungrier.

266
00:20:29,019 --> 00:20:30,770
I'm starving!

267
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:33,397
I told you!

268
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,400
Look after my little angel.

269
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:39,487
Go on without me.

270
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:44,242
Just say you'll never forget
the queer you once knew.

271
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:46,827
Look. A cemetery.

272
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:48,871
I'm not dead yet!

273
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:04,679
Now I'm alive again!

274
00:21:05,389 --> 00:21:10,309
But there's nothing for a baby
in these offerings to the dead!

275
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:12,436
We'll get by!

276
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:15,606
Yeah, sure. "We'll get by!"

277
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:19,110
People keep on saying that
till they end up living like us.

278
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:25,157
And while we keep on saying it,
the kid'll end up under a stone here.

279
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:27,034
"Kiyoko"! She has a name!

280
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:31,998
Yeah, whatever. And she's cute.
She's so pretty.

281
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:35,001
But listen to me. I'm serious.

282
00:21:35,585 --> 00:21:37,044
You listening?

283
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:41,549
If you really care about that kid,

284
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:44,802
you'll find her someone
to take care of her.

285
00:21:44,928 --> 00:21:47,430
I speak from experience.

286
00:21:47,556 --> 00:21:49,724
That's what her parents said, I bet.

287
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:53,644
What do you mean?
I wouldn't abandon a kid.

288
00:21:53,770 --> 00:21:56,063
Don't be stupid!

289
00:21:56,189 --> 00:21:59,150
No. Your family abandoned you!

290
00:21:59,735 --> 00:22:03,237
There you go again!
Am I going to sit and listen

291
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:06,324
while some dumb queer
pisses on me?

292
00:22:06,450 --> 00:22:10,536
What are we doing here? Tell me.

293
00:22:10,662 --> 00:22:12,538
Wracking our brains!

294
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:15,958
We're scavenging offerings
left in a cemetery.

295
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:19,045
And why? Because we're homeless.

296
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:22,214
- Stop it!
- No! I'm not going to stop.

297
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:25,301
We are three good-for-nothing bums

298
00:22:25,427 --> 00:22:27,887
who can't even look after ourselves.

299
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:30,389
Shut up! I'm thinking!

300
00:22:30,515 --> 00:22:32,391
I won't shut up.

301
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:37,855
You can't get milk from an old queer's
tits, no matter how hard you think.

302
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:42,234
Come on, Hana!
You know we can't do this.

303
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:44,195
Speak for yourself!

304
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:47,281
This way, the whole family will be dead.

305
00:22:56,124 --> 00:22:57,958
Oh, my!

306
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:01,712
You're so lucky, Kiyoko!

307
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:03,964
God must really love you!

308
00:23:05,008 --> 00:23:06,509
Then why was she...

309
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:07,968
...dumped?

310
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,554
Left!

311
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:14,683
- That's a dead end.
- It's right!

312
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:19,480
- Tails.
- Heads.

313
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:31,659
What's this guy doing, parking like that?

314
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:34,870
Doesn't he know
what a "public thoroughfare" is?

315
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,143
How did that happen?

316
00:23:57,269 --> 00:24:03,232
Bad luck. The car got stuck,
and I forgot the parking brake.

317
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:05,693
Then someone shouted,
"Dorothy, wait!"

318
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:11,365
And then I heard, "Whoops!"
and the damn car rolled on top of me.

319
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:18,956
I don't bring my men with me
when I'm visiting the old man's grave.

320
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:23,419
I owe you.
Call me if you're ever in trouble.

321
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,796
Oh, no, we never have any trouble.

322
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:27,965
You're from Kinshicho?

323
00:24:28,091 --> 00:24:30,801
We were just going there.

324
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:33,304
I know it's rude to ask.

325
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:35,556
If it's rude, then don't ask.

326
00:24:35,682 --> 00:24:37,141
Come on.

327
00:24:38,518 --> 00:24:41,395
Would you know this establishment?

328
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:42,897
CLUB SWIRL: "MIDORI"

329
00:24:44,065 --> 00:24:45,733
Know it?

330
00:24:46,568 --> 00:24:50,779
Its owner's marrying my daughter today.

331
00:24:52,073 --> 00:24:56,911
He's one of my men,
but he's too cocky.

332
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:59,455
I was against it.

333
00:24:59,581 --> 00:25:01,916
But your daughter chose him.

334
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:05,753
The daughter I brought up,
married to a man like that.

335
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:08,464
Know what I mean?

336
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:13,719
But if your daughter's
happy with him,

337
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:15,763
isn't that the main thing?

338
00:25:15,889 --> 00:25:16,972
You're right!

339
00:25:17,098 --> 00:25:24,230
I went to the old man's grave
so I wouldn't cry at the wedding.

340
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:25,856
Watch the road!

341
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:33,322
Good evening, sir!

342
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:37,284
Make yourselves at home.

343
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:52,132
Daddy, you're late!

344
00:25:52,259 --> 00:25:56,178
Sorry, sorry. I almost got killed.

345
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:59,056
I owe them my life.

346
00:25:59,182 --> 00:26:00,724
My daughter, Kiyoko.

347
00:26:00,850 --> 00:26:02,101
Oh. Hello.

348
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:15,614
What have you gotten us into?

349
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,992
Just shut up and eat!

350
00:26:21,663 --> 00:26:24,415
Diaper change. Your turn, Miyuki.

351
00:26:32,757 --> 00:26:37,094
Don't you think
Kiyoko has amazing luck?

352
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:40,639
Yeah.

353
00:26:41,349 --> 00:26:43,309
Maybe she does.

354
00:26:46,813 --> 00:26:49,481
Oh, yeah. Her name's Sachiko.

355
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:51,358
Not "Midori"?

356
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:53,068
Just at the club.

357
00:26:53,194 --> 00:26:56,030
She's Sachiko, "happy child,"
though she didn't look it.

358
00:26:56,156 --> 00:27:01,160
But some plastic surgery turned her
into a good little earner.

359
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:05,623
She quit.
Said she was pregnant.

360
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:07,625
Do you know where she is?

361
00:27:08,501 --> 00:27:11,003
I doubt you'll wring
any money out of her.

362
00:27:11,755 --> 00:27:14,548
No, I have something to give her.

363
00:27:18,386 --> 00:27:22,097
I'm sorry I spilled your food.

364
00:27:22,223 --> 00:27:25,476
You remember her?
Midori, the skinny broad.

365
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:29,521
She said her husband was in debt.

366
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,774
What's wrong with you?

367
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,233
That bastard.

368
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:35,569
Do you know him?

369
00:27:36,112 --> 00:27:38,155
Then she borrowed
more money from us,

370
00:27:38,281 --> 00:27:41,492
and ended up screwed both ways.

371
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:43,577
You know where she is?

372
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:47,956
If it weren't for his damn
get-rich-quick scheme,

373
00:27:48,083 --> 00:27:50,918
I'd still be with my wife and kid!

374
00:27:51,044 --> 00:27:53,671
But aren't they both dead?

375
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:55,923
I'll kill the bastard!

376
00:27:56,966 --> 00:27:59,134
You'll get killed!

377
00:28:25,870 --> 00:28:27,287
Mitsuo! Mitsuo!

378
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,707
It was that maid!

379
00:28:29,833 --> 00:28:31,709
Are you okay?

380
00:28:32,794 --> 00:28:34,169
She's got a gun!

381
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:36,839
Hey, what?

382
00:28:41,886 --> 00:28:43,679
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

383
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:45,806
Hey!

384
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:10,581
Thank you very much.

385
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:13,792
She's got a gun, you know!

386
00:29:13,918 --> 00:29:17,421
- Our lives are already wasted!
- Hana!

387
00:29:22,802 --> 00:29:23,761
There!

388
00:29:49,412 --> 00:29:53,749
Yes! One of your cabs picked up
a young woman with a baby.

389
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:56,794
Number 12-25. Send it to...

390
00:29:57,962 --> 00:30:00,881
...the Tokyo Tower.
My name is...

391
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:06,053
Hey! Wait a minute.

392
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:15,062
We're homeless bums,
not action-movie heroes.

393
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:17,523
What we need now is the police.

394
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:23,570
If you like the police so much,
get them to adopt you!

395
00:30:23,696 --> 00:30:26,448
Those children are like family!

396
00:30:26,574 --> 00:30:28,742
I thought I could depend on you!

397
00:30:28,868 --> 00:30:32,246
Don't talk like you were my damn wife.

398
00:30:34,582 --> 00:30:36,208
I'm not going anywhere.

399
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:37,459
Gin!

400
00:30:37,919 --> 00:30:40,128
We've done all we could.

401
00:30:40,255 --> 00:30:41,380
You're giving up?

402
00:30:42,423 --> 00:30:45,217
There's nothing we can do.

403
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:48,470
You really are the lowest of the low!

404
00:30:48,596 --> 00:30:51,765
The best thing you'll ever do
is die in the gutter!

405
00:30:51,891 --> 00:30:55,686
Oh, poor you!
You'll be dead and no one'll care!

406
00:30:55,812 --> 00:30:58,689
All you ever do is cause people trouble!

407
00:30:58,815 --> 00:31:01,441
Dead or alive, you're living trash!

408
00:31:01,568 --> 00:31:04,278
The king of trash!

409
00:31:08,491 --> 00:31:12,828
Okay, so I'm trash. But you're ugly.

410
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:32,347
- Yes?
- I want to get rid of some trash.

411
00:31:37,687 --> 00:31:40,105
I don't think I'd fit.

412
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:45,861
Yeah, that's what I am, living trash!

413
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:51,742
Who cares if you die in the gutter?

414
00:31:52,952 --> 00:31:56,580
You're dead all the same.

415
00:32:18,770 --> 00:32:20,729
You okay?

416
00:32:21,522 --> 00:32:23,899
Hang in there, Gramps.

417
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:29,696
- May I make one last request?
- What?

418
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:33,700
Give me a drink of that.

419
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:27,045
You're not selling me into slavery!

420
00:33:29,048 --> 00:33:31,216
Somebody, help!

421
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:49,609
I always wanted to die drunk,
in a nice old house.

422
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:52,904
Now I'm halfway there.

423
00:33:53,031 --> 00:33:55,157
Fate works in strange ways.

424
00:33:56,159 --> 00:33:58,994
I've lived a long time,

425
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:02,914
but I'm just trash,
as worthless dead as alive.

426
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:05,167
Don't talk like that!

427
00:34:06,002 --> 00:34:10,172
You remind me of myself
when I was younger.

428
00:34:10,757 --> 00:34:13,467
Looking at you now,

429
00:34:13,593 --> 00:34:16,720
may I make a last request?

430
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:20,474
Get rid of this for me.

431
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:26,313
Some people will be hurt
if it's known who I am.

432
00:34:26,439 --> 00:34:30,067
Okay. I understand.
No one will ever know.

433
00:34:43,998 --> 00:34:48,293
Take care of yourself, okay?
May I make a last...?

434
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,253
Request?

435
00:34:56,010 --> 00:34:58,720
And now, goodbye.

436
00:35:14,070 --> 00:35:15,112
That's it!

437
00:35:18,282 --> 00:35:20,075
Thanks, Gramps!

438
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:28,542
Time for the New Year's clean-up!

439
00:35:37,051 --> 00:35:38,802
Big breasts... Cool!

440
00:35:52,525 --> 00:35:54,025
Husband?

441
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:12,085
Father... Police.

442
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:14,171
Your dad's a cop?

443
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:17,507
- My father was a policeman!
- Father, policeman?

444
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:25,390
Except I'm the one
he's going to be arresting.

445
00:36:40,448 --> 00:36:41,656
Hold it.

446
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:47,287
Hi! How've you been?

447
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:51,917
Now? Just cleaning up.

448
00:36:52,043 --> 00:36:54,211
Hey, wake up!

449
00:36:54,337 --> 00:36:55,420
Come on!

450
00:36:58,925 --> 00:37:00,759
No! Not that!

451
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:03,929
Time to die, old man!

452
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:07,015
Kiyo's coming? I'm there!

453
00:37:07,725 --> 00:37:10,143
The girls are drinking near here.

454
00:37:10,269 --> 00:37:11,811
Yeah?

455
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:15,232
All cleaned up.

456
00:37:19,612 --> 00:37:21,112
Give it back!

457
00:37:22,156 --> 00:37:24,115
Give me that back!

458
00:37:25,826 --> 00:37:30,538
Her foreigner husband looked like
he was in a real bad mood.

459
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:32,582
Did he hit her?

460
00:37:32,708 --> 00:37:36,086
No, she was being real nice
for a girl so young.

461
00:37:36,212 --> 00:37:39,422
My wife could learn something!

462
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:43,635
His foreign assailant fled, taking
a young woman and a baby hostage.

463
00:37:43,761 --> 00:37:49,140
With the groom in serious condition,
police speculate this may be a war

464
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:51,476
between crime syndicates.

465
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:54,688
Hey, this is serious!

466
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:56,773
I'm not kidding around, either!

467
00:38:03,406 --> 00:38:05,573
My mum's religious.

468
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:07,867
She chants all the time.

469
00:38:13,791 --> 00:38:14,874
Me.

470
00:38:19,213 --> 00:38:21,339
Isn't she cute?

471
00:38:21,465 --> 00:38:24,718
I found her. Those spots
on her back look like wings.

472
00:38:24,844 --> 00:38:27,470
So I called her "Angel".

473
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:30,515
But she's gone.

474
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:34,811
Father.

475
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:47,365
I stabbed my father.

476
00:38:47,491 --> 00:38:49,868
I can never go back.

477
00:39:16,228 --> 00:39:19,064
The baby? A gift from God.

478
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:25,320
Give me a break.
I've got a family at home.

479
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:27,822
Those children are my family!

480
00:39:29,992 --> 00:39:31,701
They went in there.

481
00:39:32,328 --> 00:39:34,746
- Hey! The fare!
- I'll be right back.

482
00:39:34,872 --> 00:39:37,165
Miyuki! Kiyoko!

483
00:39:38,542 --> 00:39:40,543
Miyuki! Kiyoko!

484
00:39:40,669 --> 00:39:42,337
Where are you?

485
00:39:49,553 --> 00:39:52,430
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

486
00:40:09,198 --> 00:40:11,574
How could you do this to me?

487
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:14,536
It's your own fault!

488
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:18,498
You never listen to anything I say!

489
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:22,669
Use the scarf I made you
to mop up the blood!

490
00:40:22,795 --> 00:40:24,254
What have you done with Angel?

491
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:27,048
Where is she? Where is my Angel?

492
00:40:27,716 --> 00:40:30,844
She's right here. Our angel.

493
00:40:33,139 --> 00:40:36,433
I'm hungry.
Make me some food.

494
00:40:37,685 --> 00:40:41,479
Why? What are you doing
in my house?

495
00:40:41,605 --> 00:40:45,817
Miyuki, take Kiyoko. I'll get dinner.

496
00:40:56,162 --> 00:41:00,957
Kiyoko! Miyuki!

497
00:41:06,046 --> 00:41:07,338
Uncle Bag?

498
00:41:11,177 --> 00:41:14,762
Oh, I've missed you, my little angel!

499
00:41:18,517 --> 00:41:22,270
I wish I was her mother,
but I'm just another queer.

500
00:41:23,606 --> 00:41:27,775
Miyuki...
I'm so glad you're safe.

501
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:38,912
Where's the geezer?

502
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:41,456
He could be dead, for all I care!

503
00:41:44,043 --> 00:41:46,586
I'm dying.

504
00:41:56,430 --> 00:41:58,848
Maybe he went home.

505
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:00,475
Who cares?

506
00:42:00,601 --> 00:42:02,894
All he thinks about is himself.

507
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:09,150
Yeah, Miss Hana, but you're in love
with him, aren't you?

508
00:42:09,276 --> 00:42:13,196
Don't be silly!
I like my men to be more "manly".

509
00:42:13,322 --> 00:42:18,826
The kind of man I like is slender,
middle-aged, tanned,

510
00:42:18,953 --> 00:42:22,539
with a divine square-back haircut
and a lower-town accent

511
00:42:22,665 --> 00:42:25,708
who says, "Ah, what the hell,"

512
00:42:25,834 --> 00:42:29,003
when I don't quite have the cab fare.

513
00:42:32,341 --> 00:42:34,801
So, what now, Miss Hana?

514
00:42:34,927 --> 00:42:39,222
Why are you calling me that?
"Uncle Bag" is fine.

515
00:42:39,348 --> 00:42:41,516
It's hard to say.

516
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:50,024
I'm glad.

517
00:42:53,070 --> 00:42:54,237
He just died there?

518
00:42:54,363 --> 00:42:55,822
He was homeless.

519
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:57,407
I might be next.

520
00:42:57,533 --> 00:42:58,783
Just do your job.

521
00:42:58,909 --> 00:43:00,952
Gin!

522
00:43:03,664 --> 00:43:06,040
Gin! Gin!

523
00:43:06,750 --> 00:43:08,334
Take it easy.

524
00:43:08,460 --> 00:43:09,460
Gin!

525
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:11,087
Calm down!

526
00:43:19,638 --> 00:43:23,349
Where is that man of mine?

527
00:43:24,476 --> 00:43:29,063
Kiyo...

528
00:43:30,107 --> 00:43:34,777
If only tonight...

529
00:43:36,155 --> 00:43:40,366
I wanted to see you before I died.

530
00:43:42,995 --> 00:43:45,622
Kiyoko!

531
00:44:01,305 --> 00:44:05,016
What is your desire?
My magic, or an ambulance?

532
00:44:05,976 --> 00:44:09,020
- An ambulance.
- Well! Aren't you rude?

533
00:44:10,230 --> 00:44:14,525
What are we going to do?
Kiyoko can't sleep out on the street!

534
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:18,863
The geezer's not here,
we're freezing, sleepy, hungry.

535
00:44:18,989 --> 00:44:20,490
This sucks!

536
00:44:21,158 --> 00:44:23,826
I guess there's no choice.

537
00:44:29,583 --> 00:44:32,085
I never thought I'd be here again.

538
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:42,720
I'm sorry. We're closed
for a private party tonight...

539
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:46,474
Hana?

540
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:50,645
I know I have no right
to come strolling in now,

541
00:44:50,771 --> 00:44:54,649
but there's no one else
I can call on, "Mother"!

542
00:44:59,279 --> 00:45:00,905
Hana!

543
00:45:01,615 --> 00:45:02,949
Mother!

544
00:45:03,075 --> 00:45:04,409
Hana!

545
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:13,084
Geezer?

546
00:45:16,422 --> 00:45:18,256
What happened, Gin?

547
00:45:20,676 --> 00:45:23,261
Some kids beat me up.

548
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:27,098
I guess I'm just not an action hero.

549
00:45:31,395 --> 00:45:34,063
He said he knew you.

550
00:45:34,189 --> 00:45:37,442
But he said he was homeless,
you know.

551
00:45:38,485 --> 00:45:39,902
So am I.

552
00:45:40,028 --> 00:45:43,740
What? But why?

553
00:45:44,950 --> 00:45:47,243
Since Ken died, I'm like a canary

554
00:45:47,369 --> 00:45:49,996
that's forgotten its song.

555
00:45:50,122 --> 00:45:52,415
You sing all the time!

556
00:45:54,251 --> 00:45:55,668
Isn't she cute?

557
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:57,628
I wish I could have one!

558
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:06,262
So Ken died, did he?

559
00:46:08,265 --> 00:46:09,682
AIDS?

560
00:46:10,142 --> 00:46:12,393
He slipped on the soap.

561
00:46:12,519 --> 00:46:16,481
Well, death is always
a hair's breadth away.

562
00:46:17,065 --> 00:46:21,110
But if you were in trouble,
why didn't you come back?

563
00:46:23,906 --> 00:46:27,283
We certainly had fun here, didn't we?

564
00:46:29,077 --> 00:46:31,704
In this old bar

565
00:46:31,830 --> 00:46:35,333
I've had so much to drink

566
00:46:36,251 --> 00:46:38,336
My old memories

567
00:46:39,004 --> 00:46:43,466
All start to blur

568
00:46:43,592 --> 00:46:46,010
My lover

569
00:46:46,136 --> 00:46:49,472
Has left me

570
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:55,978
People call me notorious

571
00:46:56,104 --> 00:46:57,939
Aw, you're ugly!

572
00:46:58,440 --> 00:47:00,942
Good for nothing

573
00:47:01,068 --> 00:47:01,943
Get off!

574
00:47:02,069 --> 00:47:04,737
Good for nothing

575
00:47:05,739 --> 00:47:09,492
What a terrible thing to say

576
00:47:09,618 --> 00:47:12,078
Eat shit, you old fart!

577
00:47:13,705 --> 00:47:17,625
"Shit" I'll take, but "fart" I won't!

578
00:47:24,800 --> 00:47:28,261
I couldn't come back after I'd done that.

579
00:47:28,387 --> 00:47:32,306
A little bit of money took care of that.

580
00:47:32,432 --> 00:47:35,142
I'm just happy you're all right.

581
00:47:37,187 --> 00:47:40,398
Stop it!
You scare me when you start crying.

582
00:47:42,401 --> 00:47:46,612
What about that baby?
ls the girl its mother?

583
00:47:46,738 --> 00:47:47,989
Well...

584
00:47:51,451 --> 00:47:54,912
Where is your mother, anyway?

585
00:47:55,956 --> 00:47:57,164
Abandoned?

586
00:47:57,291 --> 00:48:00,710
Yes! I've been abandoned!

587
00:48:03,213 --> 00:48:05,840
Them's the breaks, I guess.

588
00:48:07,593 --> 00:48:10,219
I could see me in her.

589
00:48:10,345 --> 00:48:14,557
Born on the street,
and back there again.

590
00:48:15,017 --> 00:48:20,730
That's why I want to find her
a home full of love!

591
00:48:20,856 --> 00:48:25,276
All I ever wanted was love!

592
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:33,284
Ow!

593
00:48:39,958 --> 00:48:41,834
What the hell?

594
00:48:44,463 --> 00:48:47,006
The geezer's come out.

595
00:48:47,132 --> 00:48:48,507
Where are my clothes?

596
00:48:58,310 --> 00:49:00,144
Way to go, Gin!

597
00:49:01,980 --> 00:49:04,148
Come back any time.

598
00:49:05,275 --> 00:49:07,693
Thank you, Mother.

599
00:49:10,781 --> 00:49:17,286
My mother's white breath as she watches me
set out on a long journey.

600
00:50:33,113 --> 00:50:35,823
Oh, man!

601
00:50:35,949 --> 00:50:39,452
An empty building's always nice,
but look who got here first.

602
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:46,584
I'd just love to fill up on some meat!

603
00:50:47,169 --> 00:50:49,045
Don't you dare!

604
00:50:50,714 --> 00:50:53,174
Just kidding!

605
00:50:57,888 --> 00:51:01,432
The snow's let up.
Miyuki, will you go shopping?

606
00:51:01,558 --> 00:51:02,600
Okay.

607
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:04,935
Get me some sake.

608
00:51:05,562 --> 00:51:07,271
Just one.

609
00:51:25,290 --> 00:51:27,625
- No!
- I wish.

610
00:51:44,810 --> 00:51:46,185
"Honey, I'm home."

611
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:10,126
You stayed in there?
You'd think you were homeless!

612
00:52:14,589 --> 00:52:17,925
Actually, we're looking for these people.

613
00:52:19,427 --> 00:52:21,679
Sachiko Nishizawa.

614
00:52:22,139 --> 00:52:23,389
Do you know her?

615
00:52:23,890 --> 00:52:27,643
She never paid me back for
her Neighbourhood Association dues.

616
00:52:27,769 --> 00:52:30,146
Are you a relative?

617
00:52:30,272 --> 00:52:35,109
No! We're acquaintances of a relative.

618
00:52:35,235 --> 00:52:37,444
Her husband was no better.

619
00:52:37,571 --> 00:52:42,074
Gambling day and night,
and mean when he drank.

620
00:52:44,119 --> 00:52:47,288
Living on his wife's earnings
and borrowed money.

621
00:52:47,414 --> 00:52:49,206
Where are they now?

622
00:52:49,332 --> 00:52:53,002
I wouldn't know.
Mrs Kurumizawa might.

623
00:52:53,503 --> 00:52:56,714
They left about three months ago.

624
00:52:57,716 --> 00:53:04,471
The house was seized for debt.
One night they just up and went.

625
00:53:05,265 --> 00:53:08,517
They were a nice couple at first,

626
00:53:08,643 --> 00:53:12,605
but it wasn't long
before they started fighting.

627
00:53:12,731 --> 00:53:14,773
That's poverty for you.

628
00:53:14,900 --> 00:53:19,153
All that debt didn't stop him
from lording it over her.

629
00:53:19,279 --> 00:53:22,907
Even the most dedicated wife
has her limits.

630
00:53:24,034 --> 00:53:26,118
You'd see bruises sometimes.

631
00:53:26,244 --> 00:53:28,078
The poor woman.

632
00:53:28,205 --> 00:53:30,581
Not on her, on him!

633
00:53:30,707 --> 00:53:31,957
Oh, dear!

634
00:53:32,834 --> 00:53:39,590
But his mother would always
take his side against her.

635
00:53:40,675 --> 00:53:43,510
His parents built them this house.

636
00:53:43,637 --> 00:53:47,598
- Where do they live?
- Mrs Yamanouchi might know.

637
00:53:49,935 --> 00:53:52,311
Her mother-in-law
was always complaining

638
00:53:52,437 --> 00:53:54,647
that she never did any housework.

639
00:53:54,773 --> 00:53:57,024
But her son was perfect, of course.

640
00:53:57,150 --> 00:53:59,902
Of course! That's why I told her

641
00:54:00,028 --> 00:54:04,073
she'd never see a grandchild
with his wife working in a club.

642
00:54:04,616 --> 00:54:07,534
But she did get pregnant.

643
00:54:07,661 --> 00:54:09,912
Well, a man and a woman...

644
00:54:10,038 --> 00:54:13,999
They can always find time
to do what they must!

645
00:54:14,125 --> 00:54:17,086
SHINKOCHO 1-2-25,
MAISON HAPPINESS, APT. 203

646
00:54:18,838 --> 00:54:21,215
What if they ran out
from this new place too?

647
00:54:21,341 --> 00:54:23,842
What a horrible man!

648
00:54:23,969 --> 00:54:29,306
Poor Sachiko! Working to pay off
her husband's gambling debts!

649
00:54:29,432 --> 00:54:30,849
Right.

650
00:54:30,976 --> 00:54:35,688
But I never thought
of abandoning the kid.

651
00:54:35,814 --> 00:54:38,023
- Huh?
- Nothing.

652
00:54:38,149 --> 00:54:42,319
That's no reason to just dump the kid.

653
00:54:42,445 --> 00:54:44,071
I've said that all along.

654
00:54:47,242 --> 00:54:51,620
MIYUKI: ANGEL HAS COME HOME.
DAD.

655
00:54:56,126 --> 00:54:59,044
Doesn't it ever get tired of snowing?

656
00:55:01,589 --> 00:55:03,424
Thank you.

657
00:55:13,101 --> 00:55:16,562
I wonder how we look to them.

658
00:55:16,688 --> 00:55:19,356
Like a bum, a queer,
a runaway and a foundling.

659
00:55:19,899 --> 00:55:23,319
Kiyoko is God's messenger.
We're her servants.

660
00:55:24,529 --> 00:55:27,031
Unpaid servants.

661
00:55:27,157 --> 00:55:30,326
Paying for a father's sins.

662
00:55:30,452 --> 00:55:33,787
Yeah, if her father had been
any good at all,

663
00:55:33,913 --> 00:55:36,206
we wouldn't be going through all this.

664
00:55:37,917 --> 00:55:43,047
Even a good-for-nothing father
never forgets a child.

665
00:55:45,091 --> 00:55:46,925
I'm going out.

666
00:55:51,056 --> 00:55:53,807
What's the matter with her?

667
00:55:53,933 --> 00:55:57,353
A child never forgets its parents.

668
00:56:02,108 --> 00:56:08,989
I never stop wanting
to see my daughter, just once.

669
00:56:09,115 --> 00:56:11,408
So she's alive?

670
00:56:11,534 --> 00:56:12,785
Yeah.

671
00:56:12,911 --> 00:56:14,078
And your wife?

672
00:56:15,330 --> 00:56:20,167
I'm sure she's remarried
and living happily.

673
00:56:25,465 --> 00:56:28,717
Hello. It's me, Miyuki.

674
00:56:29,469 --> 00:56:31,553
Why did you split up?

675
00:56:31,679 --> 00:56:33,764
- Drinking and gambling.
- What?

676
00:56:35,016 --> 00:56:36,350
Just like...

677
00:56:37,435 --> 00:56:39,728
I'm a louse.

678
00:56:40,855 --> 00:56:46,110
But I've always wanted to do
something for her as a father,

679
00:56:46,236 --> 00:56:48,320
even just a little.

680
00:56:48,446 --> 00:56:52,533
When I was gambling,
this would have been nothing.

681
00:56:52,659 --> 00:56:56,245
Now I've had to sweat blood
just to save 30,000 yen.

682
00:56:56,371 --> 00:56:58,789
That's great, Gin!

683
00:56:58,915 --> 00:57:02,209
- We can stuff ourselves!
- Stuff you!

684
00:57:11,803 --> 00:57:13,220
Ishida speaking.

685
00:57:22,063 --> 00:57:25,149
Miyuki? Is that you?

686
00:57:27,318 --> 00:57:29,319
Are you all right?

687
00:57:34,701 --> 00:57:36,160
I'm sorry!

688
00:57:36,286 --> 00:57:37,953
I'm sorry!

689
00:57:38,538 --> 00:57:40,330
I'm sorry!

690
00:57:42,584 --> 00:57:45,085
Excuse me,
but if you wouldn't mind.

691
00:57:45,211 --> 00:57:47,087
"Get out," you mean?

692
00:57:47,213 --> 00:57:50,883
Other customers might like to sit down.

693
00:57:51,009 --> 00:57:54,219
- There's hardly anyone here...
- You guys stink!

694
00:57:54,971 --> 00:57:58,557
What are you?
Homeless or something?

695
00:58:03,813 --> 00:58:05,981
Who are you looking at?

696
00:58:08,026 --> 00:58:09,443
Hold it, you!

697
00:58:14,324 --> 00:58:18,619
Hold it, I said, you low-life!

698
00:58:24,125 --> 00:58:27,836
It's New Year's Sale time
at The Food Store!

699
00:58:27,962 --> 00:58:34,384
Come to The Food Store
for all your special New Year's needs!

700
00:58:34,511 --> 00:58:37,221
See in the New Year with your family!

701
00:58:37,347 --> 00:58:39,139
Call an ambulance, quick.

702
00:58:39,891 --> 00:58:41,308
Right!

703
00:58:44,479 --> 00:58:49,191
I knew it! Kiyoko really is
the messenger of God!

704
00:58:51,819 --> 00:58:53,737
- Hey!
- Miss Hana!

705
00:58:53,863 --> 00:58:55,280
Hey!

706
00:58:55,406 --> 00:58:56,448
Hana!

707
00:59:12,715 --> 00:59:15,467
Following a recent gangland
shooting incident,

708
00:59:15,593 --> 00:59:21,181
police are seeking a fugitive
thought to be Latin American.

709
00:59:21,808 --> 00:59:24,560
Mitsuo Hiruta, shot three times,

710
00:59:24,686 --> 00:59:28,730
in protecting the leader
of his syndicate,

711
00:59:28,856 --> 00:59:34,069
will be questioned
after he recovers from his wounds.

712
00:59:34,988 --> 00:59:38,657
Isn't she cute!
When was she born?

713
00:59:38,783 --> 00:59:41,994
Not long ago, I guess.

714
00:59:42,120 --> 00:59:43,704
So the mother...?

715
00:59:43,830 --> 00:59:45,372
I'm not.

716
00:59:45,957 --> 00:59:48,375
- What's her name?
- Kiyoko.

717
00:59:48,501 --> 00:59:52,421
That's my name too.
What a coincidence.

718
00:59:55,091 --> 00:59:57,509
Your friend is very weak.

719
00:59:57,635 --> 01:00:00,554
Make sure he gets rest
and proper nutrition.

720
01:00:00,680 --> 01:00:01,930
Doctor!

721
01:00:02,807 --> 01:00:05,309
Believe it or not, we're homeless.

722
01:00:05,435 --> 01:00:07,644
I'm just a doctor.

723
01:00:09,063 --> 01:00:14,610
Rest and nutrition don't fit
with our lifestyle, you realise.

724
01:00:15,570 --> 01:00:21,742
I can try to cure disease.
Lifestyle is something you have to fix.

725
01:00:21,868 --> 01:00:25,120
All anyone can do is their best.

726
01:00:27,540 --> 01:00:29,291
Take care.

727
01:00:32,879 --> 01:00:36,048
The bill for today is 29,830 yen.

728
01:00:36,174 --> 01:00:40,385
Bring your health-insurance card
and you'll get a refund.

729
01:00:41,554 --> 01:00:44,014
I'm sorry, Gin!

730
01:00:44,766 --> 01:00:48,352
Stop crying!
You'll get the bills all wet.

731
01:00:49,062 --> 01:00:51,063
That's 30,000 yen.

732
01:01:07,330 --> 01:01:08,664
Kiyoko?

733
01:01:13,711 --> 01:01:14,753
Dad?

734
01:01:37,694 --> 01:01:39,778
So you took up nursing.

735
01:01:41,114 --> 01:01:43,281
I see.

736
01:01:45,702 --> 01:01:47,619
I'm glad you're well.

737
01:01:47,745 --> 01:01:53,208
Oh, yeah, I'm just great.
How's your mother?

738
01:01:53,334 --> 01:01:54,584
Fine.

739
01:01:55,503 --> 01:01:57,671
Yeah? That's good.

740
01:01:58,256 --> 01:02:00,006
What are you doing now?

741
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:06,430
I'm in recycling.
I had to drop something off here.

742
01:02:10,476 --> 01:02:12,185
You must hate me.

743
01:02:13,771 --> 01:02:18,024
I was never
any kind of a father to you.

744
01:02:18,151 --> 01:02:24,072
But that 30,000 yen was money
I'd saved up for you.

745
01:02:25,575 --> 01:02:27,075
You may not believe it.

746
01:02:30,455 --> 01:02:33,749
I always wanted to see you.

747
01:02:35,042 --> 01:02:39,337
When I was little,
Mum and I searched for you.

748
01:02:39,464 --> 01:02:42,090
We even checked unidentified corpses.

749
01:02:43,050 --> 01:02:47,429
After you disappeared,
Mum ran the store herself.

750
01:02:48,681 --> 01:02:49,473
The store?

751
01:02:49,599 --> 01:02:53,769
It was hard for a woman
to run a bicycle shop alone.

752
01:02:54,771 --> 01:02:57,898
That's not quite the same
as a bicycle racer.

753
01:02:58,024 --> 01:03:04,196
The man you owed money to was shot
and wounded the other day, you know.

754
01:03:04,322 --> 01:03:05,781
He lived?

755
01:03:06,824 --> 01:03:08,867
That's a relief.

756
01:03:08,993 --> 01:03:10,994
I thought you'd say that.

757
01:03:13,873 --> 01:03:18,794
I ran up the debts, not him.

758
01:03:20,421 --> 01:03:24,966
Thank that doctor for me.
He seems like a nice guy.

759
01:03:25,885 --> 01:03:28,303
I'm getting married.

760
01:03:30,181 --> 01:03:31,932
Oh? That's good.

761
01:03:32,058 --> 01:03:33,350
To him.

762
01:03:33,476 --> 01:03:37,938
Great! But isn't he about my age?

763
01:03:38,564 --> 01:03:42,317
He's been married.
His daughter got sick and died,

764
01:03:42,902 --> 01:03:45,153
and his wife followed her.

765
01:03:50,409 --> 01:03:52,244
That man makes me so mad!

766
01:03:52,370 --> 01:03:53,995
Aren't you moved?

767
01:03:54,914 --> 01:03:58,834
- Here's the address and phone number.
- Yours?

768
01:03:58,960 --> 01:04:01,419
The old house is gone.

769
01:04:01,546 --> 01:04:03,922
Even if you can't now,
call me sometime.

770
01:04:05,091 --> 01:04:07,467
Kiyoko!

771
01:04:09,512 --> 01:04:13,640
I've had about all I can stand!

772
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:17,435
- Miss Hana?
- Telling us you were a racer!

773
01:04:18,437 --> 01:04:20,480
I was always at the track.

774
01:04:20,606 --> 01:04:21,982
Yeah, betting!

775
01:04:22,108 --> 01:04:26,444
And your debts snowballed
so you couldn't face your family

776
01:04:26,571 --> 01:04:28,488
and you ran and hid in a cardboard box!

777
01:04:28,614 --> 01:04:30,365
Yes, damn it!

778
01:04:30,491 --> 01:04:32,993
That's what your father is!

779
01:04:33,452 --> 01:04:37,163
He can't bet, he's spineless,
his feet stink and he can't drink!

780
01:04:37,290 --> 01:04:41,167
He kills off his wife and daughter
to buy sympathy!

781
01:04:41,294 --> 01:04:44,170
He said you had an incurable disease!

782
01:04:44,297 --> 01:04:49,718
With a father like that,
you have my sympathy!

783
01:04:49,844 --> 01:04:53,054
Is this how you repay me?

784
01:04:53,180 --> 01:04:54,931
Repay you?

785
01:04:55,057 --> 01:04:57,058
Am I hearing right?

786
01:04:57,184 --> 01:04:59,394
If we're talking about debt,
I'm waiting for my change!

787
01:04:59,520 --> 01:05:02,063
Debt's a concept
you don't even understand!

788
01:05:02,189 --> 01:05:05,775
You understand how to troll
through garbage cans!

789
01:05:05,902 --> 01:05:08,778
And how to get in debt
and how to make babies.

790
01:05:08,905 --> 01:05:12,449
Though you're not too good
at raising them, are you?

791
01:05:12,575 --> 01:05:15,577
And your debts
you shove off on your wife.

792
01:05:15,703 --> 01:05:19,080
Always running away,
never doing anything right!

793
01:05:19,206 --> 01:05:22,000
Running away's
the only racing you ever did!

794
01:05:22,126 --> 01:05:25,170
Miyuki! We're leaving!

795
01:05:28,090 --> 01:05:29,382
Miss Hana?

796
01:05:34,764 --> 01:05:36,765
I guess he's better.

797
01:05:38,100 --> 01:05:41,144
Should you have said that
in front of her?

798
01:05:43,940 --> 01:05:47,233
If she's his daughter,
she'll forgive him.

799
01:05:50,154 --> 01:05:53,448
Being able to speak freely

800
01:05:53,574 --> 01:05:56,409
is the lifeblood of love.

801
01:05:57,453 --> 01:05:59,412
Maybe I'm naive.

802
01:06:01,874 --> 01:06:04,209
So you're in love with him?

803
01:06:04,335 --> 01:06:07,879
Don't be silly.
I'm the Weeping Red Devil.

804
01:06:08,005 --> 01:06:12,050
- What?
- It's a story I love.

805
01:06:12,718 --> 01:06:17,555
There was a red devil who wanted
to be friends with people.

806
01:06:18,516 --> 01:06:23,269
But since he was a devil,
no one would go near him.

807
01:06:23,396 --> 01:06:27,107
So his friend the blue devil
made a plan.

808
01:06:28,192 --> 01:06:33,697
He'd wreak havoc among the people,
and the red devil would save them.

809
01:06:38,828 --> 01:06:40,662
WHEN YOU TRY
TO ACHIEVE SOMETHING,

810
01:06:40,788 --> 01:06:42,497
SOMEONE'S BOUND TO GET HURT.

811
01:06:43,541 --> 01:06:46,167
YOU ALWAYS HAVE
TO SACRIFICE SOMETHING.

812
01:06:46,752 --> 01:06:48,962
The plan worked.

813
01:06:49,088 --> 01:06:53,967
But the blue devil had to go away,
so they'd never know it was a trick.

814
01:06:56,804 --> 01:06:58,471
It's a sad story.

815
01:06:58,597 --> 01:07:02,767
But that means you leave.
Where will you go?

816
01:07:03,644 --> 01:07:07,022
It's best for everyone
when they're with their family.

817
01:07:07,148 --> 01:07:09,190
Soon we'll find Kiyoko's mother.

818
01:07:09,316 --> 01:07:13,653
And then what?
You don't have a real family!

819
01:07:23,706 --> 01:07:27,042
RARE "LINE OF ONES"
WINS LOTTERY

820
01:07:27,168 --> 01:07:31,838
Numbers have been drawn for
the annual New Year's Jumbo Lottery.

821
01:07:32,381 --> 01:07:35,800
Top prize in the 200-million-yen
lottery is a very rare number.

822
01:07:36,552 --> 01:07:40,805
Group 11, number 111,111

823
01:07:40,931 --> 01:07:43,600
is worth 50 million yen.

824
01:07:44,268 --> 01:07:45,560
A different group pays
100,000 yen.

825
01:07:46,687 --> 01:07:50,065
To repeat,
the winning prize number is...

826
01:07:51,901 --> 01:07:53,526
This just in.

827
01:07:54,028 --> 01:07:57,614
Police have released a sketch
of an infant taken

828
01:07:57,740 --> 01:08:01,409
from a hospital
in Tokyo's Shinagawa Ward.

829
01:08:03,954 --> 01:08:08,958
We've come all the way here,
but we don't have her address!

830
01:08:09,085 --> 01:08:11,669
The geezer's got it! Let's go back.

831
01:08:11,796 --> 01:08:14,130
Where are you going?

832
01:08:15,716 --> 01:08:19,928
- The police!
- What? You hated that idea!

833
01:08:20,846 --> 01:08:22,806
I was just ego-tripping.

834
01:08:23,557 --> 01:08:26,851
Now I want to apologise
to her parents.

835
01:08:26,977 --> 01:08:31,356
They might not be able to sleep
waiting for news about her.

836
01:08:31,482 --> 01:08:35,193
That's what we said
from the very start!

837
01:08:35,319 --> 01:08:39,489
They might even be
about to commit suicide!

838
01:08:39,615 --> 01:08:43,034
I've done something
that can't be taken back!

839
01:08:43,160 --> 01:08:45,912
I'll throw myself in this river.

840
01:08:46,038 --> 01:08:50,208
I'll step neatly out of my shoes,
stand on the handrail, and be at peace.

841
01:08:50,334 --> 01:08:53,419
But then I'll see a baby's face
on the water.

842
01:08:53,546 --> 01:08:58,299
No! While I see this child's face,
I cannot die!

843
01:08:58,425 --> 01:09:00,260
Hey, you!

844
01:09:00,386 --> 01:09:01,594
No!

845
01:09:03,931 --> 01:09:07,350
- You're too young for this!
- Please! Let me die!

846
01:09:14,984 --> 01:09:16,526
You!

847
01:09:17,319 --> 01:09:19,445
Sachiko Nishizawa...

848
01:09:22,867 --> 01:09:24,868
What were you thinking of?

849
01:09:24,994 --> 01:09:27,036
Is that an apology?

850
01:09:27,163 --> 01:09:31,416
If we hadn't found this child,
she would've frozen to death!

851
01:09:31,542 --> 01:09:32,876
It wasn't me!

852
01:09:33,002 --> 01:09:36,171
My husband took her away
when I wasn't there!

853
01:09:37,381 --> 01:09:40,175
I've looked and looked!

854
01:09:47,391 --> 01:09:48,975
Is that true?

855
01:09:51,729 --> 01:09:56,941
All I've suffered
on account of that man!

856
01:10:08,204 --> 01:10:11,080
"Hi, Mum!"

857
01:10:19,089 --> 01:10:22,926
God really loves this child, you know.

858
01:10:23,052 --> 01:10:26,512
I want you to give her lots of love too.

859
01:10:26,639 --> 01:10:29,599
Do right by her, or you'll pay for it.

860
01:10:29,725 --> 01:10:31,643
I'm so sorry!

861
01:10:31,769 --> 01:10:33,019
I'm sorry!

862
01:10:43,030 --> 01:10:44,906
Mrs Nishizawa!

863
01:11:31,203 --> 01:11:34,872
What are you doing in here?
Get out of here! Get out!

864
01:11:35,416 --> 01:11:37,458
Wait! I'm no thief.

865
01:11:37,584 --> 01:11:39,961
You're lying! Get out!

866
01:11:40,087 --> 01:11:42,005
Where's the baby?

867
01:11:44,758 --> 01:11:47,969
Did an old queer and a girl come
to give it back?

868
01:11:48,095 --> 01:11:49,679
What are you talking about?

869
01:11:49,805 --> 01:11:51,931
You abandoned a baby!

870
01:11:54,143 --> 01:11:56,227
I can prove it.

871
01:11:56,687 --> 01:11:58,855
Are you a cop?

872
01:11:58,981 --> 01:12:03,568
Huh? I'm just a bum
who was passing by.

873
01:12:04,778 --> 01:12:06,863
Are you right in the head?

874
01:12:06,989 --> 01:12:09,324
I'm damn near crazy from all this!

875
01:12:09,450 --> 01:12:14,704
Why is the baby you abandoned
on the news as being "taken away"?

876
01:12:14,830 --> 01:12:17,248
They'll call us kidnappers!

877
01:12:17,833 --> 01:12:21,919
It wasn't me. That's not my kid.

878
01:12:24,173 --> 01:12:25,381
What?

879
01:12:27,259 --> 01:12:29,510
There, there! Don't cry!

880
01:12:29,636 --> 01:12:30,720
Take care.

881
01:12:31,430 --> 01:12:33,097
Raise her right.

882
01:12:33,223 --> 01:12:35,308
See you again someday.

883
01:12:36,935 --> 01:12:39,562
Never leave her again.

884
01:13:02,503 --> 01:13:10,009
On the year's last day, when all
of a life's accounts have been settled up

885
01:13:20,187 --> 01:13:24,941
Sachiko stole that baby
out of the hospital.

886
01:13:25,067 --> 01:13:29,445
She stole a baby
and then abandoned it?

887
01:13:29,571 --> 01:13:31,531
That's a person's life!

888
01:13:31,657 --> 01:13:34,283
She lied to me about it!

889
01:13:34,410 --> 01:13:37,954
And now it's got way out of control.

890
01:13:38,080 --> 01:13:42,583
I don't want anything to do with it!
Take the kid to the police!

891
01:13:42,709 --> 01:13:44,127
What?

892
01:13:45,212 --> 01:13:48,089
Don't act like you're not part of this!

893
01:13:48,215 --> 01:13:51,676
You don't want to get involved?
You're her husband!

894
01:13:51,802 --> 01:13:56,055
That's all over!
I'm getting my life back together.

895
01:13:56,181 --> 01:13:56,973
Look!

896
01:13:57,099 --> 01:14:00,893
I won 100,000 yen in the lottery.
My luck's turned!

897
01:14:04,440 --> 01:14:10,653
I know a guy just like you.
He threw away his life and his family.

898
01:14:10,779 --> 01:14:13,030
No. They threw him away.

899
01:14:13,157 --> 01:14:15,158
I'm no loser!

900
01:14:20,080 --> 01:14:22,248
These were in your wife's bag.

901
01:14:24,668 --> 01:14:28,045
Any idea where she might have gone?

902
01:14:28,172 --> 01:14:31,716
She said she was going
to be with her baby.

903
01:14:31,842 --> 01:14:34,635
She was going to kill herself!

904
01:14:36,513 --> 01:14:38,181
There's no time to waste!

905
01:14:38,307 --> 01:14:41,893
No! She was just going
to go look for the kid.

906
01:14:42,019 --> 01:14:44,479
She's desperate.
That only means one thing!

907
01:14:46,190 --> 01:14:47,648
But where do I look?

908
01:15:03,874 --> 01:15:04,916
Hana!

909
01:15:05,042 --> 01:15:06,334
Miyuki!

910
01:15:08,045 --> 01:15:09,378
Kiyoko!

911
01:15:15,677 --> 01:15:18,304
God must be busy at this time of year.

912
01:15:18,430 --> 01:15:20,723
Better once a year than never.

913
01:15:21,642 --> 01:15:22,350
Geezer?

914
01:15:31,985 --> 01:15:35,988
You're too late.
You just missed a very moving finale.

915
01:15:36,114 --> 01:15:38,074
What's the matter?

916
01:15:41,828 --> 01:15:43,162
"Kiyoko"!

917
01:15:46,291 --> 01:15:47,667
"Stomach"?

918
01:15:49,545 --> 01:15:51,128
"Mother"!

919
01:15:51,255 --> 01:15:54,173
Now that's settled,
what the hell do you mean?

920
01:15:54,675 --> 01:15:58,553
Fake! The mother! Sachiko's a fake!

921
01:16:00,764 --> 01:16:02,139
Pardon?

922
01:16:07,437 --> 01:16:10,022
Why won't you drink?

923
01:16:10,732 --> 01:16:15,194
A baby has to drink
from its mother's breast.

924
01:16:15,862 --> 01:16:19,949
We'll never be close if you don't!

925
01:16:26,373 --> 01:16:28,082
Sorry. Wrong people.

926
01:16:30,627 --> 01:16:32,587
She can't be far!

927
01:16:33,046 --> 01:16:35,006
But where do we look?

928
01:16:35,132 --> 01:16:37,758
We can't just give her up now!

929
01:16:50,731 --> 01:16:52,231
That's Kiyoko!

930
01:16:59,448 --> 01:17:01,073
Should you be running?

931
01:17:01,199 --> 01:17:03,951
If I don't run now, when will I?

932
01:17:04,077 --> 01:17:04,994
This way!

933
01:17:19,301 --> 01:17:23,262
Returning stolen goods to a thief!
How could we be so dumb?

934
01:17:23,388 --> 01:17:25,181
Who said "family suicide"?

935
01:17:25,307 --> 01:17:26,766
You did!

936
01:17:32,939 --> 01:17:33,939
- Which way?
- Left.

937
01:17:34,066 --> 01:17:36,067
- Okay, right!
- Why?

938
01:17:36,568 --> 01:17:37,902
You're a lousy gambler!

939
01:17:38,028 --> 01:17:40,112
You got that right.

940
01:17:40,238 --> 01:17:42,114
Somebody help!

941
01:17:55,796 --> 01:17:57,046
Hey!

942
01:17:57,547 --> 01:17:58,506
Wait!

943
01:17:58,632 --> 01:18:00,341
Thief! Thief!

944
01:18:00,467 --> 01:18:04,845
- What's wrong?
- A woman just stole my truck!

945
01:18:05,555 --> 01:18:06,847
Hey! Thief!

946
01:18:06,973 --> 01:18:09,100
Yes! That woman!

947
01:18:09,601 --> 01:18:12,395
She's a baby thief!

948
01:18:26,910 --> 01:18:30,204
Be quiet, will you?
Please! Be a good baby!

949
01:18:38,630 --> 01:18:40,881
Stop! Give Kiyoko back!

950
01:18:45,470 --> 01:18:47,179
Give me a break!

951
01:18:47,305 --> 01:18:49,348
I'm forever in your debt!

952
01:18:54,563 --> 01:18:55,855
Gin!

953
01:18:57,274 --> 01:18:59,400
That woman's crazy!

954
01:18:59,985 --> 01:19:00,860
Get closer!

955
01:19:00,986 --> 01:19:01,819
I can't!

956
01:19:01,945 --> 01:19:04,280
You have to, for Kiyoko!

957
01:19:04,406 --> 01:19:06,282
- Who's Kiyoko?
- Step on it like a man!

958
01:19:06,408 --> 01:19:07,533
Okay!

959
01:19:12,414 --> 01:19:15,040
Please! Be quiet!

960
01:19:18,754 --> 01:19:20,254
- Gin!
- Geezer?

961
01:19:23,759 --> 01:19:24,800
Geezer!

962
01:19:24,926 --> 01:19:28,262
Go for it, Gin!
No action star can touch you!

963
01:19:28,388 --> 01:19:29,889
Pass her!

964
01:19:30,015 --> 01:19:31,891
- We'll die!
- Step on it!

965
01:19:32,017 --> 01:19:33,559
Okay!

966
01:19:35,312 --> 01:19:37,021
Stop crying!

967
01:19:37,898 --> 01:19:40,983
Don't be afraid.
I'll never leave you again.

968
01:19:41,485 --> 01:19:42,526
You want to die?

969
01:19:51,787 --> 01:19:53,704
Gin!

970
01:20:05,759 --> 01:20:07,009
Gin!

971
01:20:09,596 --> 01:20:10,638
There!

972
01:20:12,349 --> 01:20:13,974
- Are you okay?
- Where's Kiyoko?

973
01:20:14,100 --> 01:20:15,684
- Faster!
- Okay!

974
01:20:35,372 --> 01:20:35,913
Which way?

975
01:21:23,253 --> 01:21:25,004
We're at the scene

976
01:21:25,130 --> 01:21:29,717
where a truck has crashed
into a building in Shinagawa.

977
01:21:29,843 --> 01:21:34,096
Now a woman holding a baby
has appeared on the roof.

978
01:21:34,598 --> 01:21:39,393
Witnesses say the woman
is connected with the incident

979
01:21:39,519 --> 01:21:41,770
as she was driving the truck.

980
01:21:48,069 --> 01:21:50,863
Now there's someone else on the roof!

981
01:21:55,535 --> 01:21:56,452
Stay away!

982
01:21:56,578 --> 01:21:58,787
No!

983
01:22:05,629 --> 01:22:08,088
Tell me why you took that baby.

984
01:22:08,214 --> 01:22:11,717
I didn't! This baby is mine!

985
01:22:11,843 --> 01:22:15,471
You're lying! Its real parents
are worried sick about it!

986
01:22:15,597 --> 01:22:16,805
That's not true!

987
01:22:16,932 --> 01:22:20,851
You of all people should know
what it's like to lose a child!

988
01:22:32,364 --> 01:22:37,618
She's dead. My baby died
before she was even born!

989
01:22:44,918 --> 01:22:48,712
All the other babies looked
so healthy there in the ward.

990
01:22:48,838 --> 01:22:51,382
I wanted to die.

991
01:22:51,508 --> 01:22:54,134
But then this baby smiled at me.

992
01:22:54,260 --> 01:22:56,387
I decided she was mine.

993
01:22:56,513 --> 01:23:00,641
I thought as long as I had her,
everything would be fine.

994
01:23:00,767 --> 01:23:04,478
My husband would mend his ways,
and we'd be a real family.

995
01:23:04,604 --> 01:23:06,647
That's bullshit!

996
01:23:06,773 --> 01:23:12,069
Build a family by ruining a baby's life?
If you're going to die, do it alone!

997
01:23:12,195 --> 01:23:17,032
A life is a life. It's only born once.
You, me, or Kiyoko.

998
01:23:22,622 --> 01:23:24,665
Give her back, okay?

999
01:23:32,007 --> 01:23:33,924
I want to be reborn.

1000
01:23:34,926 --> 01:23:37,011
Sachiko!

1001
01:23:38,263 --> 01:23:41,306
Sachiko, don't die!
Come back to me!

1002
01:23:41,433 --> 01:23:45,310
I was wrong!
Please, don't kill yourself!

1003
01:23:45,437 --> 01:23:49,940
We'll start again!
We'll be reborn! Sachiko!

1004
01:23:50,442 --> 01:23:53,235
I'll go first and wait for you.

1005
01:23:57,532 --> 01:23:58,782
Sachiko!

1006
01:24:01,202 --> 01:24:02,536
Please! Let me die!

1007
01:24:02,662 --> 01:24:05,748
Kiyoko wants to see her mum and dad!

1008
01:24:11,713 --> 01:24:13,130
I want to go home.

1009
01:24:16,468 --> 01:24:18,469
I'm sorry!

1010
01:24:26,478 --> 01:24:30,647
Take her to her mother and father.

1011
01:24:40,116 --> 01:24:41,742
Oh, no.

1012
01:24:41,868 --> 01:24:43,202
Hana!

1013
01:24:44,913 --> 01:24:48,082
I'm okay! I'm still alive!

1014
01:25:28,623 --> 01:25:32,668
Inspector, I don't know how to thank you.

1015
01:25:32,794 --> 01:25:36,463
We're not the ones you should thank.

1016
01:25:38,633 --> 01:25:43,679
Man, that was a good sleep!
Get me a cigarette, Miyuki.

1017
01:25:43,805 --> 01:25:46,098
- In my jacket.
- Yeah, yeah.

1018
01:25:46,224 --> 01:25:49,476
That was some New Year's!

1019
01:25:50,311 --> 01:25:52,146
It's "No Smoking" here.

1020
01:25:52,272 --> 01:25:55,440
Lighten up. I'm a hero.

1021
01:25:55,567 --> 01:25:57,693
You mean "we"!

1022
01:26:01,156 --> 01:26:06,535
I guess we won't have to listen
to Kiyoko's damn crying anymore.

1023
01:26:06,661 --> 01:26:08,912
She's not "Kiyoko" anymore.

1024
01:26:09,038 --> 01:26:11,331
I'm not pleased.

1025
01:26:12,250 --> 01:26:14,126
What can we do?

1026
01:26:14,252 --> 01:26:15,919
Not that.

1027
01:26:16,462 --> 01:26:18,630
This is a men's ward.

1028
01:26:21,467 --> 01:26:23,093
Perhaps we're intruding.

1029
01:26:23,219 --> 01:26:25,429
No, it's just...

1030
01:26:25,972 --> 01:26:28,432
I'm told they're homeless.

1031
01:26:28,558 --> 01:26:29,850
Who cares?

1032
01:26:29,976 --> 01:26:32,853
We'd like them to be her godfathers.

1033
01:26:34,647 --> 01:26:35,939
Come in.

1034
01:26:36,858 --> 01:26:37,900
Excuse us.

1035
01:26:38,651 --> 01:26:42,112
The baby's parents
would like to thank you...

1036
01:26:47,785 --> 01:26:49,119
Dad...
